asr-000069
00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:09.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, ComSec. We now officially commence this budget hearing of the Presidential Communications Operations Office and its attached agencies.

asr-000070
00:26:10.220 --> 00:26:16.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Anyway, let us now proceed with the presentation of the PCO family. Let us begin with the PCO proper.

asr-000071
00:26:17.900 --> 00:26:20.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Secretary, are you going to make a presentation?

asr-000072
00:26:21.080 --> 00:26:22.960
Secretary David M. Gomez: I will take you through the presentation.

asr-000073
00:26:22.960 --> 00:26:26.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Secretary. You have five to seven minutes. Go ahead, please.

asr-000074
00:26:27.060 --> 00:26:29.480
Secretary David M. Gomez: Thank you very much, Mr. Chairman, and good afternoon.

asr-000075
00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:45.340
Secretary David M. Gomez: Your Honor, on behalf of the Presidential Communications Office, allow me to express our sincere gratitude for the gracious invitation to appear before this committee today and for the very warm welcome extended to us here in the August halls of the Senate of the Philippines.

asr-000076
00:26:45.900 --> 00:26:56.680
Secretary David M. Gomez: It is my honor, together with the heads and officials of the PCO and our attached agencies, to present and explain our proposed budget for fiscal year 2027.

asr-000077
00:26:56.900 --> 00:26:59.680
Secretary David M. Gomez: Allow me first to provide some context for our proposed approach.

asr-000078
00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:16.540
Secretary David M. Gomez: For 2027, the PCO is proposing a budget of P2.621 billion, representing just 0.03% of the proposed P7.2 trillion national budget.

asr-000079
00:27:16.820 --> 00:27:29.820
Secretary David M. Gomez: Our proposed budget, Your Honor, is the lowest among the departments in the executive branch, yet the mandate entrusted to us are both broad and consequential.

asr-000080
00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:50.520
Secretary David M. Gomez: With this modest resources, Your Honor, the PCO and its attached agencies remain fully committed to the formidable task of engaging and informing our citizens, working with the mass media, and helping foster a more informed and meaningful public discourse on policies, programs, and actions of government.

asr-000081
00:27:50.520 --> 00:27:59.820
Secretary David M. Gomez: We therefore come before this honorable committee mindful of our responsibility to ensure that every peso entrusted to the PCO is

asr-000082
00:27:59.820 --> 00:28:29.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: used prudently, effectively, and in the service of the Filipino people. Next slide, please. Your Honor, the PCO family?s budget proposal of 2.621 billion is 6.6% lower than our current 2026 budget. As mentioned earlier, it accounts for 0.03%

asr-000083
00:28:29.820 --> 00:28:59.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: of the 7.2 trillion National Expenditure Program for 2027. Next slide, please. Per Executive Order No. 16, Your Honor, the PCO has six attached agencies and three GOCCs attached to the department. The following are the major programs, activities, and projects to be funded by our proposed 2027 national budget. Next slide, please.

asr-000084
00:28:59.820 --> 00:29:15.160
Secretary David M. Gomez: The Presidential Communications Program is at the core of our mandate to serve as the primary communication arm of the Office of the President and the Executive Branch, ensuring that government messages are clear, consistent, and accessible to the Filipino people.

asr-000085
00:29:15.160 --> 00:29:29.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: The program primarily focuses on the formulation, coordination, and implementation of integrated public information plans and programs that effectively communicate the priorities, policies, and achievements of the President and the Executive Department.

asr-000087
00:29:29.940 --> 00:29:44.620
Secretary David M. Gomez: It involves not only the crafting of messages but also the careful alignment of communication strategies across agencies to ensure coherence and clarity in how government policies and programs are conveyed to the public.

asr-000088
00:29:44.960 --> 00:29:57.140
Secretary David M. Gomez: In a time when information is fast-moving and often contested, the program ensures that our citizens receive timely, accurate, and relevant information straight from the government.

asr-000089
00:29:58.500 --> 00:29:59.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: In line with this,

asr-000091
00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:18.860
Secretary David M. Gomez: The main organizational outcome that we seek to achieve is public access, engagement, and understanding of presidential policies and government programs. This means that we are not only ensuring that information reaches the people, but also that it resonates with them and encourages meaningful dialogue.

asr-000092
00:30:18.860 --> 00:30:29.360
Secretary David M. Gomez: Through accessible and inclusive communication, we empower citizens to engage in public discourse, to raise their concerns, and to take part in nation-building.

asr-000093
00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:34.500
Secretary David M. Gomez: To realize these outcomes, we are implementing several concrete activities.

asr-000094
00:30:35.160 --> 00:30:43.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: Among these is the Freedom of Information Program, which upholds transparency by granting citizens greater access to government data and information.

asr-000095
00:30:44.100 --> 00:30:48.780
Secretary David M. Gomez: We also conduct regular press briefings to provide timely updates and clarification.

asr-000096
00:30:48.860 --> 00:31:04.940
Secretary David M. Gomez: To strengthen information literacy, we have launched the Maging Mapanuri Program, a series of fact-checking workshops designed to combat disinformation and promote responsible news consumption.

asr-000097
00:31:05.260 --> 00:31:18.720
Secretary David M. Gomez: We also undertake the coverage of presidential engagements, both local and international, ensuring that the Filipino people are kept informed of the President's activities in the country and his representation.

asr-000098
00:31:18.860 --> 00:31:34.820
Secretary David M. Gomez: Ultimately, the Presidential Communications Program positions communication as a bridge between the government and the people, a bridge built on trust, transparency, and accountability.

asr-000099
00:31:35.260 --> 00:31:47.140
Secretary David M. Gomez: It ensures that the President's policies and the administration's development agenda are not only heard, but also understood, embraced, and supported by the citizenry.

asr-000100
00:31:47.140 --> 00:31:48.840
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000101
00:31:48.860 --> 00:31:55.880
Secretary David M. Gomez: Now we present, Your Honor, the programs of the attached agencies of the PCO.

asr-000102
00:31:56.620 --> 00:32:09.200
Secretary David M. Gomez: First, under the Bureau of Broadcast Services, we implement the Public Radio Broadcasting Program, which ensures nationwide access to timely and relevant information through radio.

asr-000103
00:32:09.880 --> 00:32:18.840
Secretary David M. Gomez: Second, under the Bureau of Communication Services, we carry out the Government Communications Program, which produces print, audiovisual, and digital materials

asr-000106
00:32:18.920 --> 00:32:25.740
Secretary David M. Gomez: that amplify government policies, projects, and services for public awareness and understanding.

asr-000107
00:32:26.440 --> 00:32:41.780
Secretary David M. Gomez: Third, the News and Information Bureau is responsible for providing efficient, effective, productive, and economical services relating to the development and formulation of domestic and foreign information programs of the government.

asr-000108
00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:43.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000109
00:32:44.920 --> 00:32:48.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: Fourth is the National Printing Office, which oversees the national printing.

asr-000110
00:32:48.860 --> 00:33:18.840
Secretary David M. Gomez: Fifth is the Philippine Information Agency, which implements the development communication programs of the government, bringing information closer to the people through regional and provincial networks while promoting citizen participation and grassroots engagement.

asr-000111
00:33:18.860 --> 00:33:37.620
Secretary David M. Gomez: Finally, Radio TV Malacanang, or RTVM, manages the Presidential Documentation and Broadcast Management Program, which provides full coverage broadcast and archiving of the President's official activities and public engagements, both local and international.

asr-000112
00:33:37.620 --> 00:33:48.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: Together, these programs from our attached agencies ensure a comprehensive, multi-platform communication system that allows the government to effectively reach and engage our people.

asr-000113
00:33:48.860 --> 00:33:50.700
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000114
00:33:51.580 --> 00:33:58.600
Secretary David M. Gomez: We wish to emphasize, Your Honor, that the PCO has consistently been achieving its financial and physical targets.

asr-000115
00:33:59.420 --> 00:34:07.340
Secretary David M. Gomez: The PCO proper's Congress-approved performance indicators, targets, and budget allocation under the GAA are shown on the succeeding slides.

asr-000116
00:34:07.960 --> 00:34:14.540
Secretary David M. Gomez: These targets are achieved through the synergy and collaboration of the various operating units of the PCO proper.

asr-000117
00:34:15.240 --> 00:34:16.200
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000127
00:34:18.860 --> 00:34:44.200
Secretary David M. Gomez: I am pleased to report, Your Honor, that the agency has achieved and exceeded all targets for its performance indicators under the fiscal year 2025 General Appropriations Act. This achievement is largely attributed to strengthened media partnerships under the current administration, which led to increased access and more events being attended by the media, both locally and abroad. Next slide, please.

asr-000128
00:34:44.200 --> 00:34:48.500
Secretary David M. Gomez: For the PCO proper's financial performance,

asr-000129
00:34:48.500 --> 00:34:49.680
Secretary David M. Gomez: for 2025,

asr-000130
00:34:50.520 --> 00:35:00.220
Secretary David M. Gomez: 84.79% of the obligated funds under all available appropriations last year were already disbursed or paid for.

asr-000131
00:35:01.040 --> 00:35:03.700
Secretary David M. Gomez: As of December 31, 2025,

asr-000132
00:35:04.240 --> 00:35:13.400
Secretary David M. Gomez: more than 87.51% of our released appropriations in the 2025 GAA were obligated or utilized.

asr-000133
00:35:13.400 --> 00:35:15.720
Secretary David M. Gomez: For fiscal year 2025,

asr-000134
00:35:16.560 --> 00:35:18.400
Secretary David M. Gomez: the unobligated allotments and unpaid appropriations

asr-000135
00:35:18.500 --> 00:35:24.400
Secretary David M. Gomez: are attributed mainly to the intervening factors in the implementation of its programs,

asr-000136
00:35:24.900 --> 00:35:31.880
Secretary David M. Gomez: i.e. procurement bottlenecks and the transition activities conducted in relation to the change in top leadership.

asr-000137
00:35:32.820 --> 00:35:37.680
Secretary David M. Gomez: The PCO experienced financial performance challenges during the subject fiscal year

asr-000138
00:35:37.680 --> 00:35:40.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: due to procurement delays and adjustments in priorities

asr-000139
00:35:40.640 --> 00:35:46.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: following the assumption of the new management in February and again in July 2025.

asr-000140
00:35:46.640 --> 00:35:50.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000141
00:35:50.640 --> 00:36:04.160
Secretary David M. Gomez: The agency has again achieved and exceeded all its physical targets this time for the first semester of 2026 and is on track to achieve all its targets for the rest of the year.

asr-000142
00:36:04.160 --> 00:36:14.320
Secretary David M. Gomez: This was done through strategic resource utilization, streamlined workflows, and strong team coordination despite structural and staffing limitations.

asr-000143
00:36:15.200 --> 00:36:16.420
Secretary David M. Gomez: Productivity was maximized by the PCO.

asr-000144
00:36:16.420 --> 00:36:19.140
Secretary David M. Gomez: The agency has also optimized by developing targeted innovations,

asr-000145
00:36:19.360 --> 00:36:23.380
Secretary David M. Gomez: including communicating presidential events in the vernacular

asr-000146
00:36:23.380 --> 00:36:28.060
Secretary David M. Gomez: and strengthening stakeholder partnerships for seamless media coverage.

asr-000147
00:36:29.380 --> 00:36:30.660
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000148
00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:34.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: For our mid-year performance,

asr-000149
00:36:35.040 --> 00:36:43.180
Secretary David M. Gomez: we have already obligated 26.17% of our available appropriations as of June 30 or mid-year this year,

asr-000150
00:36:43.180 --> 00:36:46.180
Secretary David M. Gomez: out of which 92.11% have been allocated.

asr-000151
00:36:46.420 --> 00:36:48.980
Secretary David M. Gomez: We have already been paid for or disbursed.

asr-000152
00:36:49.840 --> 00:36:51.980
Secretary David M. Gomez: Please note that for fiscal year 2026,

asr-000153
00:36:52.600 --> 00:37:00.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: PCO has an agency-specific appropriation under its own budget in the GAA amounting to around 953.9 million

asr-000154
00:37:00.800 --> 00:37:05.500
Secretary David M. Gomez: and another fund for ASEAN 2026 Summit Hosting

asr-000155
00:37:05.500 --> 00:37:13.160
Secretary David M. Gomez: pursuant to the Special Provision No. 1 of the OP Properties Budget where it is lodged under the GAA.

asr-000156
00:37:13.160 --> 00:37:13.320
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000163
00:37:13.500 --> 00:37:17.600
Secretary David M. Gomez: For the first semester of 2026,

asr-000164
00:37:17.720 --> 00:37:24.400
Secretary David M. Gomez: the unobligated allotments were primarily attributed to the issuance of Memorandum Circular 114

asr-000165
00:37:24.400 --> 00:37:31.140
Secretary David M. Gomez: which directed all national government agencies to strictly implement energy conservation measures

asr-000166
00:37:31.140 --> 00:37:36.700
Secretary David M. Gomez: in response to the rising global oil and electricity crisis as a result of the Middle East conflict.

asr-000167
00:37:36.700 --> 00:37:42.700
Secretary David M. Gomez: In addition, the ASEAN National Organizing Council directed the recalibration

asr-000170
00:37:43.600 --> 00:37:49.160
Secretary David M. Gomez: the recalibration and downsizing to bare bones of preparatory meetings

asr-000171
00:37:49.160 --> 00:37:55.180
Secretary David M. Gomez: with activities to be conducted through virtual platforms whenever feasible.

asr-000172
00:37:56.660 --> 00:37:57.860
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000173
00:38:01.560 --> 00:38:10.180
Secretary David M. Gomez: May we note, Your Honor, that the PCO proper returned to the DBM 95.758 million

asr-000174
00:38:10.180 --> 00:38:12.740
Secretary David M. Gomez: from its fiscal year 2026 allotment.

asr-000175
00:38:12.740 --> 00:38:21.380
Secretary David M. Gomez: This is pursuant to DBM National Budget Circular 602 and 603 issued in response to the National Energy Emergency

asr-000176
00:38:21.380 --> 00:38:28.980
Secretary David M. Gomez: and to augment funds for PAPs intended to mitigate the economic and social impact of the Middle East conflict.

asr-000177
00:38:29.520 --> 00:38:36.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Secretary, let me just ask you, you said you returned 9 point something billion or million?

asr-000178
00:38:36.720 --> 00:38:37.840
Secretary David M. Gomez: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-000179
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:39.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: To the National Treasury?

asr-000180
00:38:39.420 --> 00:38:42.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I was wondering.

asr-000181
00:38:42.740 --> 00:38:43.120
Secretary David M. Gomez: 95.

asr-000182
00:38:43.480 --> 00:38:50.120
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I was wondering why you had a reduction in your budget for 2026.

asr-000183
00:38:50.240 --> 00:38:52.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: You had 953 and now it's 765.

asr-000184
00:38:54.760 --> 00:38:55.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay.

asr-000185
00:38:55.680 --> 00:39:01.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Siguro naisip nila masyado matipid ang PCO kaya bawasan na lang natin.

asr-000186
00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:02.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Go ahead.

asr-000187
00:39:02.520 --> 00:39:03.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Please continue your presentation.

asr-000188
00:39:04.020 --> 00:39:10.020
Secretary David M. Gomez: Your Honor, if I may just clarify, it was really required under the National Energy Emergency Declaration of the President

asr-000189
00:39:10.020 --> 00:39:12.020
Secretary David M. Gomez: for us to cost cut and return.

asr-000190
00:39:12.740 --> 00:39:13.400
Secretary David M. Gomez: Some funds to the DBM.

asr-000191
00:39:13.400 --> 00:39:16.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Later on, I will be asking you yung inyong disbursement rate.

asr-000192
00:39:17.200 --> 00:39:18.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How is it going?

asr-000193
00:39:18.420 --> 00:39:18.640
Secretary David M. Gomez: Yes, sir.

asr-000194
00:39:18.640 --> 00:39:24.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi usually based on experience, binabawasan ng DBM ang budget ng isang ahensya

asr-000195
00:39:24.300 --> 00:39:26.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: pag nakita nila matipid masyado.

asr-000196
00:39:27.280 --> 00:39:28.160
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, go ahead.

asr-000197
00:39:28.280 --> 00:39:29.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Continue your presentation, Secretary.

asr-000198
00:39:30.160 --> 00:39:30.700
Secretary David M. Gomez: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-000199
00:39:32.420 --> 00:39:34.300
Secretary David M. Gomez: May we note that the PCO...

asr-000200
00:39:34.300 --> 00:39:35.440
Secretary David M. Gomez: Well, next slide, please.

asr-000201
