Secretary David M. Gomez: updated Philippine Development Plan for 2023 to 2028, and fiscal year 2027 budget priorities framework set by the DBM. Next slide, please. This includes the following priority or flagship programs and projects as part of the PCO?s budgetary thrust for fiscal year 2027.

asr-000223
00:41:37.720 --> 00:41:40.720
Secretary David M. Gomez: Number one, the reinforced national government infrastructure.

asr-000224
00:41:41.080 --> 00:41:50.200
Secretary David M. Gomez: By maintaining sustained engagement, including strategic briefings with key partners and strengthened operational support,

asr-000225
00:41:50.620 --> 00:41:56.080
Secretary David M. Gomez: the program directly aligns government communications with core national priorities.

asr-000226
00:41:56.780 --> 00:42:05.520
Secretary David M. Gomez: In doing so, it enhances the government's ability to deliver clear, coherent, and timely messaging to both domestic and international audiences.

asr-000227
00:42:06.160 --> 00:42:10.520
Secretary David M. Gomez: Ultimately, this approach reinforces transparency, fosters strong relationships,

asr-000228
00:42:11.080 --> 00:42:20.880
Secretary David M. Gomez: and fulfills the PCO's mandate to effectively communicate policies, programs, and official positions across the executive branch.

asr-000229
00:42:21.880 --> 00:42:27.520
Secretary David M. Gomez: Number two is the Intensified Media and Information Literacy Program.

asr-000230
00:42:27.860 --> 00:42:37.100
Secretary David M. Gomez: This program strengthens the public capacity to critically assess, analyze, and produce information in an increasingly complex media environment.

asr-000231
00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:41.060
Secretary David M. Gomez: Through targeted training, workshops, and national engagement,

asr-000233
00:42:41.100 --> 00:42:46.580
Secretary David M. Gomez: including capacity building for educators, journalists, and government communicators.

asr-000234
00:42:46.800 --> 00:42:56.200
Secretary David M. Gomez: The initiative aims to combat misinformation and disinformation, promote responsible media consumption, and rebuild public trust.

asr-000235
00:42:57.060 --> 00:43:05.520
Secretary David M. Gomez: Third is our multisectoral campaign to fight fake news, or what we call OPLAN Kontra Fake News in the PCO.

asr-000236
00:43:05.720 --> 00:43:10.600
Secretary David M. Gomez: This initiative aims to protect the public from disinformation and misinformation,

asr-000237
00:43:11.060 --> 00:43:24.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: By maintaining the credibility and integrity of information, stopping the proliferation of fake news, and strengthening the role of mass media as a trusted institution in the face of the growing power of social media.

asr-000238
00:43:24.800 --> 00:43:37.920
Secretary David M. Gomez: As such, the PCO signed a memorandum of cooperation with the country's nine national broadsheets to work together in preventing the spread of fake news and disinformation.

asr-000239
00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:55.740
Secretary David M. Gomez: By empowering the public to discern facts from falsehoods and truth from lies and holding purveyors of fake news accountable, the PCO's OPLAN contra fake news campaign strengthens freedom of speech and the public's right to information.

asr-000240
00:43:56.080 --> 00:44:07.740
Secretary David M. Gomez: This program includes the creation of an anti-fake news desk, a dedicated mechanism where its partners in the public can report suspicious or misleading information.

asr-000241
00:44:07.920 --> 00:44:20.800
Secretary David M. Gomez: Reports are promptly evaluated and referred to appropriate agencies, including the Department of Information and Communications Technology and the Department of Justice for Proper Action.

asr-000242
00:44:20.800 --> 00:44:36.500
Secretary David M. Gomez: It also integrates emerging themes such as artificial intelligence, science communications, and cyber e-gov preparedness to ensure that stakeholders are equipped to navigate the evolving information ecosystem.

