Senator Erwin Tulfo: May ngumunguya, pangit, mamaya-maya yung VIP natin, nangungulangot,

asr-002056
01:49:11.560 --> 01:49:13.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: iwasan natin kasi hindi maganda.

asr-002057
01:49:14.500 --> 01:49:19.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya marami na nga tayong kalaban, yun ho, ipi-play up nila sa video nila.

asr-002058
01:49:19.520 --> 01:49:24.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Di ho ba? I mean, Secretary Dave, yun ipi-play up ng mga kalaban para masama tignan.

asr-002059
01:49:24.800 --> 01:49:26.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Eh, kawawa naman ho.

asr-002060
01:49:27.000 --> 01:49:28.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, it's just a manifestation.

asr-002061
01:49:30.220 --> 01:49:34.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mas maganda ho yung coverage natin. Piliin natin yung mga videos natin.

asr-002062
01:49:35.100 --> 01:49:37.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Huwag lang tira lang, tira lalo po yung mga camera.

asr-002063
01:49:37.600 --> 01:49:41.520
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I'm sure sanay naman po sila sa mga ika nga presidential coverage, di po ba?

asr-002064
01:49:42.420 --> 01:49:47.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Lalo na po sa mga parties like that, may mga events.

asr-002065
01:49:47.480 --> 01:49:51.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi po hindi alam natin ang VIP na may sumusunod sa kanya na camera, di po ba?

asr-002066
01:49:51.220 --> 01:49:54.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, ang may kasalanan po doon, yung camera man,

asr-002067
01:49:54.800 --> 01:49:58.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: director na nagbibigay na nagsiswitch na pan mo sa kanan,

asr-002068
01:49:58.900 --> 01:50:00.560
Senator Erwin Tulfo: babahan mo ng konti, kaliwa mo,

asr-002069
01:50:00.980 --> 01:50:04.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: oops, si VIP natin, di magandang pwesto yan, di magandang angulo,

asr-002070
01:50:05.000 --> 01:50:07.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: alisin mo dyan, lipat muna tayo switch.

asr-002071
01:50:07.280 --> 01:50:10.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ilang cameras po ba ang ginagamit yung isang coverage, sir?

asr-002072
01:50:10.860 --> 01:50:15.420
RTVM Undersecretary Franz Gerard R. Imperial: Sa isang coverage, sir, kung maliit na coverage po, normally is three.

asr-002073
01:50:16.200 --> 01:50:17.300
RTVM Undersecretary Franz Gerard R. Imperial: Yan ang pinakaminimo.

asr-002074
01:50:17.300 --> 01:50:21.120
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sa mga events po, mga parties na pinupuntahan po ng Pangulo,

asr-002075
01:50:21.320 --> 01:50:24.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: mga ika nga ceremony, mga ilan ho ang daladalan yung camera,

asr-002076
01:50:24.800 --> 01:50:25.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: mga camera dyan.

asr-002077
01:50:26.000 --> 01:50:28.560
RTVM Undersecretary Franz Gerard R. Imperial: Bigger events, mga four lang po.

asr-002078
01:50:29.000 --> 01:50:31.880
RTVM Undersecretary Franz Gerard R. Imperial: Pero ang pinakamarami po namin normally is Sona.

asr-002079
01:50:32.700 --> 01:50:35.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Pero may mga direct contact po, yung mga camera man yun,

asr-002080
01:50:35.800 --> 01:50:39.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: kasi nakakita ko po dahil may communications, di po ba?

asr-002081
01:50:39.340 --> 01:50:42.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: At meron po director na ikita niya kung anong magandang angulo.

asr-002082
01:50:42.500 --> 01:50:44.260
RTVM Undersecretary Franz Gerard R. Imperial: Definitely, sir, meron naman po.

asr-002083
01:50:44.280 --> 01:50:48.460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Baka pwede po natin maiwasan na ho yung magagandang pangit ho na angulo minsan,

asr-002084
01:50:48.580 --> 01:50:49.320
Senator Erwin Tulfo: yung VIP natin.

asr-002085
01:50:49.440 --> 01:50:53.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Hindi lang po yung president of first family, pati mga secretaries natin,

asr-002086
01:50:53.540 --> 01:50:54.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: minsan baka mamaya.

asr-002087
01:50:54.800 --> 01:50:56.760
Senator Erwin Tulfo: May ginagawa, hindi po maganda na.

asr-002088
01:50:58.400 --> 01:51:00.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Unconsciously, akala nila walang video coverage.

asr-002089
01:51:00.880 --> 01:51:02.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yun pala, nakukunan na ho sila.

asr-002090
01:51:03.320 --> 01:51:06.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: At this day and age, nako, mabilis po pick-uping agad yan.

asr-002091
01:51:07.120 --> 01:51:09.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Bagamat hindi po fake news yan, yun ay pe-play up.

asr-002092
01:51:09.760 --> 01:51:13.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kawawa naman ho yung ating ika nga subject.

asr-002093
01:51:14.700 --> 01:51:19.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Tapos sasabihin, kita mo, kita mo, tala itong ginawa niya, di ba?

asr-002094
01:51:20.500 --> 01:51:22.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kung mali na ho, hindi na maganda tignan.

asr-002095
01:51:22.980 --> 01:51:24.640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Iwasan na ho natin, let's avoid.

asr-002096
01:51:24.800 --> 01:51:25.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ano po?

asr-002097
01:51:25.880 --> 01:51:28.660
RTVM Undersecretary Franz Gerard R. Imperial: This is something we'll continuously improve po.

asr-002098
01:51:29.000 --> 01:51:32.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi I'm still watching coverages of RTBM, PTV.

asr-002099
01:51:34.380 --> 01:51:35.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Binabantayan ko.

asr-002100
01:51:35.360 --> 01:51:36.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Secretary Dave, okay?

asr-002101
01:51:36.640 --> 01:51:38.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Can you remind our people?

asr-002102
01:51:38.420 --> 01:51:39.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi hindi maganda tignan.

asr-002103
01:51:40.080 --> 01:51:41.120
Secretary David M. Gomez: Well noted, your chair.

asr-002104
01:51:41.420 --> 01:51:41.760
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alright.

asr-002105
01:51:42.340 --> 01:51:45.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ma'am, Asek Zapata.

asr-002106
01:51:45.640 --> 01:51:48.920
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yun po, may mga unobligated pa ba tayo dyan?

asr-002107
01:51:49.020 --> 01:51:51.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Bakit parang mabagal po yung ating obligation?

asr-002108
01:51:51.440 --> 01:51:52.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ma'am?

asr-002109
01:51:53.440 --> 01:51:54.480
PCO Assistant Secretary Atty. Ronadale M. Zapata: Your honor,

asr-002110
01:51:54.800 --> 01:51:55.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: sino po sasagot?

asr-002111
01:51:56.100 --> 01:51:56.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yusek?

asr-002112
01:51:56.640 --> 01:51:57.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay, Yusek Sestoso.

asr-002113
01:51:58.560 --> 01:51:59.980
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair.

asr-002114
01:52:00.380 --> 01:52:07.100
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: For PCO, we have a budget utilization rate of 42.55,

asr-002115
01:52:07.360 --> 01:52:11.940
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: which is equivalent to 637 million and change.

asr-002116
01:52:12.400 --> 01:52:14.700
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: So, our unobligated is around,

asr-002117
01:52:15.760 --> 01:52:18.920
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: we still have 860 million.

asr-002118
01:52:20.380 --> 01:52:21.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As of?

asr-002119
01:52:21.260 --> 01:52:22.260
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: In the pipeline.

asr-002120
01:52:22.700 --> 01:52:24.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: As of today?

asr-002121
01:52:24.040 --> 01:52:28.420
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: As of September 15, Mr. Chair.

asr-002122
01:52:28.700 --> 01:52:30.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We only have three months, ma'am.

asr-002123
01:52:31.140 --> 01:52:36.660
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How do you plan to dispose that or disperse that in 90 days?

asr-002124
01:52:37.400 --> 01:52:38.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alaka, nakikinig po ang DBM.

asr-002125
01:52:39.380 --> 01:52:40.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: DBM, take note, ma'am.

asr-002126
01:52:41.320 --> 01:52:42.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yes, ma'am.

asr-002127
01:52:44.220 --> 01:52:50.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Before I continue, I would like to acknowledge the presence of Senator Villanueva.

asr-002128
01:52:51.100 --> 01:52:52.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Do you have a statement?

asr-002129
01:52:52.500 --> 01:52:53.200
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mr. Chairman,

asr-002130
01:52:54.040 --> 01:52:58.680
Senator Joel Villanueva: I will not give a long statement just to put on record my sincerest thanks and gratitude

asr-002131
01:52:58.680 --> 01:53:04.080
Senator Joel Villanueva: to our co-public officials for their service.

asr-002132
01:53:04.600 --> 01:53:08.400
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'm here to give my support.

asr-002133
01:53:08.840 --> 01:53:15.220
Senator Joel Villanueva: It's just that I have one concern and I think it was already tackled in this committee.

asr-002134
01:53:15.380 --> 01:53:19.540
Senator Joel Villanueva: I wasn't here because I had two budget hearings.

asr-002135
01:53:19.540 --> 01:53:23.540
Senator Joel Villanueva: I sponsored a bill in the...

asr-002136
01:53:24.040 --> 01:53:28.260
Senator Joel Villanueva: the plenary and God knows the kind of schedule we are having, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002137
01:53:28.660 --> 01:53:34.180
Senator Joel Villanueva: I just wanted to make sure yung dun sa APO lang, yung dun sa passport, no?

asr-002138
01:53:34.260 --> 01:53:36.220
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I think it was already mentioned about...

asr-002139
01:53:36.220 --> 01:53:37.340
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi ko po uulitin.

asr-002140
01:53:37.700 --> 01:53:43.420
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang sa akin lang, Mr. Chairman, is kung masasubsidize ng gobyerno yung increase

asr-002141
01:53:43.420 --> 01:53:47.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: kesa mag-increase kahit nga huwag lang ngayong taon o pwede mo naman next year

asr-002142
01:53:47.440 --> 01:53:50.980
Senator Joel Villanueva: magkaroon lang ng another option.

asr-002143
01:53:50.980 --> 01:53:53.980
Senator Joel Villanueva: If we can subsidize it through this...

asr-002144
01:53:54.040 --> 01:53:57.920
Senator Joel Villanueva: General Appropriations Act, masubsidize.

asr-002145
01:53:58.100 --> 01:54:04.080
Senator Joel Villanueva: Tapos sa susunod na lang i-increase, pwede rin.

asr-002146
01:54:04.220 --> 01:54:06.440
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang sa akin lang, may options tayo available for us.

asr-002147
01:54:06.660 --> 01:54:10.020
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just to put that on record, Mr. Chairman, I will no longer belabor the issue

asr-002148
01:54:10.020 --> 01:54:15.760
Senator Joel Villanueva: and I'm here to support the Secretary kahit na tagal na hoon namin kayo niyintay sa CA.

asr-002149
01:54:15.760 --> 01:54:23.760
Senator Joel Villanueva: But anyway, of course, our brother in Christ, Brad Lino, has been a good friend of mine since...

asr-002150
01:54:24.040 --> 01:54:26.000
Senator Joel Villanueva: What? For the past 30 years.

asr-002151
01:54:26.440 --> 01:54:31.940
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, maraming salamat po, Mr. Chairman. I'm here to support you and the PCO. Salamat po.

asr-002152
01:54:32.600 --> 01:54:36.320
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you, Sen. Joel Villanueva. Thank you, sir.

asr-002153
01:54:37.060 --> 01:54:39.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ma'am, continue. Yuseca Sistoso.

asr-002154
01:54:40.220 --> 01:54:51.120
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: Mr. Chair, for the second semester of 2026, our unobligated allotment will mostly be funded

asr-002155
01:54:52.160 --> 01:54:53.120
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: through the...

asr-002156
01:54:54.040 --> 01:55:01.460
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: ASEAN expenditures for the 49th Summit. So, that will cover the IMC...

asr-002157
01:55:01.460 --> 01:55:08.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Most of these remain for the ASEAN. And the highlight will be like around November. Tama po ba?

asr-002158
01:55:08.520 --> 01:55:09.340
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-002159
01:55:09.380 --> 01:55:09.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alright.

asr-002160
01:55:10.320 --> 01:55:11.660
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: So, historically...

asr-002161
01:55:11.660 --> 01:55:18.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, expecting na yung natitira po ninyo about what is left of your budget, like probably 80%,

asr-002162
01:55:18.040 --> 01:55:19.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: will be used for the ASEAN?

asr-002163
01:55:20.120 --> 01:55:23.480
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: Most likely, Your Honor, because we will be spending for the international...

asr-002164
01:55:23.480 --> 01:55:23.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alright.

asr-002165
01:55:24.040 --> 01:55:33.920
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: ...media center for accommodations, catering, and transportation. And we are also working

asr-002166
01:55:33.920 --> 01:55:43.180
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: in tandem with DOT because they will also be presenting, posting exhibits, and they will

asr-002167
01:55:43.180 --> 01:55:52.080
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: be showcasing regional exhibits, showcasing the Philippines, Luzon, Visayas, including

asr-002168
01:55:52.080 --> 01:55:53.740
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: Luzon, Visayas, and Mindanao.

asr-002169
01:55:54.040 --> 01:56:02.720
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: We will be assisting them in providing space, in providing utility consumptions, in whatever

asr-002170
01:56:02.720 --> 01:56:10.200
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: means that we can, transportation, to help them fund. Because these additional expenditures

asr-002171
01:56:10.200 --> 01:56:23.040
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: are not originally included in their budget. So, with that, most of the budget that is

asr-002172
01:56:23.040 --> 01:56:23.920
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: remaining...

asr-002173
01:56:24.040 --> 01:56:32.260
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: ...will be allocated for that. And of course, we still have advertising budget and projects

asr-002174
01:56:32.260 --> 01:56:41.240
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: of the Secretary prioritized for the second semester. And historically, Mr. Chair, PCO

asr-002175
01:56:41.240 --> 01:56:52.260
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: has a budget utilization rate of about 88% year in, year out. And most of that is spent

asr-002176
01:56:52.260 --> 01:56:53.620
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: during the second part of the year.

asr-002178
01:56:54.040 --> 01:57:01.580
PCO Undersecretary Atty. Ruth Abigail C. Sestoso: Because most of our projects are allocated during the second half.

asr-002179
01:57:01.960 --> 01:57:08.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right. Thank you, Yusec Sestoso. Let me now direct my question to Mon Ilagan, a friend of mine.

asr-002180
01:57:10.380 --> 01:57:10.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yes.

asr-002181
01:57:12.480 --> 01:57:14.920
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sorry, Mr. Chairman. I have so many friends here.

asr-002182
01:57:15.020 --> 01:57:15.320
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I know.

asr-002183
01:57:15.600 --> 01:57:16.900
Senator Joel Villanueva: Si Jim Paul, si Catherine.

asr-002184
01:57:17.040 --> 01:57:17.560
Senator Joel Villanueva: Idol ko yan.

asr-002185
01:57:17.780 --> 01:57:18.120
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: Thank you, thank you.

asr-002186
01:57:18.120 --> 01:57:18.980
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Puputin na rin ang buhok.

asr-002187
01:57:19.200 --> 01:57:21.380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Taga-USTe rin yan, eh, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002188
01:57:21.780 --> 01:57:22.620
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: Good afternoon, Your Honor.

asr-002189
01:57:22.620 --> 01:57:24.020
Senator Joel Villanueva: Maraming taga-USTe dito

asr-002190
01:57:24.040 --> 01:57:35.160
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yeah, Yusek Mon, yung inyong strategic media campaign, kasama po ba ito dun sa ikang To Combat Fake News po?

asr-002191
01:57:35.860 --> 01:57:39.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Are you also involved in this program?

asr-002192
01:57:40.220 --> 01:57:42.820
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: Yes, definitely, Your Honor. Good afternoon.

asr-002193
01:57:43.920 --> 01:57:52.540
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: Ang trabaho po ng strategic media campaigns, aside from that, is to also assist the Secretary in all the media strategies

asr-002194
01:57:52.540 --> 01:57:53.480
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: and, of course, the campaigns.

asr-002195
01:57:53.480 --> 01:58:00.600
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: The campaigns regarding the president's directives, programs, and all the programs of the different agencies.

asr-002196
01:58:00.940 --> 01:58:08.600
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: And part of the responsibility or the role of the strategic media campaigns is to really help and assist the secretary

asr-002197
01:58:08.600 --> 01:58:14.760
PCO Undersecretary Ramon A. Ilagan: in fighting the fake news, disinformation, and misinformation against the public.

asr-002198
01:58:15.280 --> 01:58:16.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right, thank you for that.

asr-002199
01:58:17.300 --> 01:58:22.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Secretary Dave, before we let you go, I want you to submit.

asr-002200
01:58:23.480 --> 01:58:25.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Your wish list, your priority.

asr-002201
01:58:25.920 --> 01:58:39.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: One of those is for IBC 13 and your priority projects that we can probably deal with during the bicameral conference

asr-002202
01:58:39.060 --> 01:58:43.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: when the two congresses will meet sometime in November.

asr-002203
01:58:43.560 --> 01:58:47.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So I would appreciate if you could submit us your wish list.

asr-002204
01:58:47.680 --> 01:58:52.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: We may not be able to give you what you wanted, like an additional 1.247,

asr-002208
01:58:53.720 --> 01:58:58.160
Senator Erwin Tulfo: billion, but we'll try to do it closer than that.

asr-002209
01:58:58.960 --> 01:59:04.020
Secretary David M. Gomez: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chairman, and we really appreciate the support of the committee.

asr-002210
01:59:04.660 --> 01:59:08.980
Secretary David M. Gomez: Sinabi ko nga po kanina, kung hindi natin ma-re-restore yung budget ng IBC 13,

asr-002211
01:59:09.440 --> 01:59:12.460
Secretary David M. Gomez: sadly, baka mag-off the air na po kami ng January 1st.

asr-002212
01:59:12.980 --> 01:59:15.380
Secretary David M. Gomez: Ganon din po yung rental ng PIA.

asr-002213
01:59:16.060 --> 01:59:18.460
Secretary David M. Gomez: Kung hindi po mababudgetan yung rental ng PIA,

asr-002214
01:59:18.460 --> 01:59:22.780
Secretary David M. Gomez: eh sa January 1st, mga squatters na rin po sila mag-inagawa yung building nila.

asr-002215
01:59:23.240 --> 01:59:23.340
Secretary David M. Gomez: So,

asr-002216
01:59:23.480 --> 01:59:26.160
Secretary David M. Gomez: ganon po ka-urgent talaga yung need namin to restore that.

asr-002217
01:59:26.220 --> 01:59:27.960
Secretary David M. Gomez: But we will provide the committee, Your Honor,

asr-002218
01:59:28.080 --> 01:59:32.980
Secretary David M. Gomez: with the list of our request for restoration of the budget from the net.

asr-002219
01:59:33.220 --> 01:59:34.580
Secretary David M. Gomez: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chairman. Thank you.

asr-002220
01:59:34.600 --> 01:59:36.620
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Director Abrillantes, we just saved you, ha?

asr-002221
01:59:37.040 --> 01:59:42.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Already said, we'll probably find some money during our buy-come

asr-002222
01:59:42.280 --> 01:59:44.460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: para medyo mabawas-bawasan po.

asr-002223
01:59:44.460 --> 01:59:49.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alam ko po na maraming agencies, sinahabol ka kayo ngayon at sinisisi.

asr-002224
01:59:49.960 --> 01:59:53.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya pati yung si Secretary natin, medyo namumuti na rin ang book

